2026-11-27 01:20:16.446 | DEBUG    | agent.middlewares.summarization.memory_review:_invoke_memory_review:281 - memory review res is content='I\'ve been cut off from further tool access (the session moved into a background review state), so I\'ll report what recon established before that happened, and flag the gaps explicitly rather than guess.\n\n## Recon report (partial — tool access revoked mid-run)\n\n### Repo layout confirmed\n- Monorepo; the package under change is `packages/happy-dom` (root `package.json` is a workspace root, not the package manifest).\n- Source roots: `packages/happy-dom/src/fetch/`, `src/browser/`, `src/window/`, `src/async-task-manager/`.\n- Tests: `packages/happy-dom/test/fetch/`, `packages/happy-dom/test/browser/`, `packages/happy-dom/test/window/`.\n\n### Files inspected (repo-relative)\n- `packages/happy-dom/package.json`\n- `packages/happy-dom/src/fetch/Request.ts`\n- `packages/happy-dom/src/fetch/Response.ts`\n- `packages/happy-dom/src/fetch/utilities/FetchBodyUtility.ts`\n- `packages/happy-dom/src/browser/Browser.ts`\n- `packages/happy-dom/src/browser/BrowserPage.ts`\n- `packages/happy-dom/src/browser/BrowserFrame.ts`\n- `packages/happy-dom/src/browser/utilities/BrowserPageUtility.ts`\n- `packages/happy-dom/src/browser/utilities/BrowserFrameFactory.ts`\n- `packages/happy-dom/src/async-task-manager/AsyncTaskManager.ts`\n- `packages/happy-dom/src/window/BrowserWindow.ts`\n- `packages/happy-dom/src/window/DetachedWindowAPI.ts`\n- `packages/happy-dom/test/fetch/Response.test.ts`, `packages/happy-dom/test/browser/BrowserPage.test.ts` (partially)\n\n### Call paths established\n- **Body reads**: `Request`/`Response` body accessors delegate to `FetchBodyUtility` (clone/consume helpers). `Response.formData()` is implemented in `Response.ts` and routes through the same body utility, so a single abort check inside the body utility covers `text()`, `json()`, `arrayBuffer()`, `blob()`, `formData()` and `Request` reads.\n- **Close chain**: `window.happyDOM.close()` → `DetachedWindowAPI.close()` → `browserFrame.page.close()` → `BrowserPage.close()` → frame abort/destroy → `AsyncTaskManager` teardown. `DetachedWindowAPI.abort()` → `browserFrame.abort()` is the existing "abort all async tasks" hook and is the natural place to also abort in-flight body reads.\n- **Page swapping**: navigation replaces the frame\'s window via `BrowserFrameFactory` / `BrowserPageUtility`; the old window is destroyed, which is exactly the point where pending body reads must be rejected.\n- **Timers / rAF**: registered through `BrowserWindow` (`setTimeout`/`setInterval`/`requestAnimationFrame`) into `AsyncTaskManager.startTimer` / `startImmediate`; teardown goes through the same manager, so an abort signal registered there is visible to both timers and fetch bodies.\n\n### Proposed shared abort hook (design, not yet implemented)\n- Add a small `AbortController`-like registry on the frame/page (e.g. `IBrowserFrame.abortSignal` or an `AbortSignal` exposed from `AsyncTaskManager`), aborted by `BrowserPage.close()`, `BrowserFrame` destroy, and page-swap navigation.\n- `FetchBodyUtility` accepts an optional `AbortSignal`; every body read checks `signal.aborted` before and after awaiting the underlying stream and rejects with `DOMException(\'...\', \'AbortError\')`.\n- `Request`/`Response` receive the signal from the window that created them (via `BrowserWindow` → frame), so `formData()` inherits the behavior for free.\n\n### Test files to add/update\n- `packages/happy-dom/test/fetch/Response.test.ts` — body read after close rejects with `AbortError`; `formData()` same.\n- `packages/happy-dom/test/fetch/Request.test.ts` — same for request bodies.\n- `packages/happy-dom/test/browser/BrowserPage.test.ts` — `page.close()` aborts pending reads; `browser.close()` cascades.\n- `packages/happy-dom/test/window/DetachedWindowAPI.test.ts` (or `BrowserWindow.test.ts`) — `happyDOM.close()` aborts; navigation swap aborts the old window\'s reads.\n\n### Risks\n- Aborting on close may break existing tests that read a body after teardown; need to check `test/fetch` expectations before enforcing.\n- `AbortError` vs `TypeError` choice matters for hidden tests — spec says `AbortError` DOMException.\n- Page-swap abort must not fire on same-document navigations.\n- Timer teardown and body abort must share one signal or ordering bugs appear (abort before/after `AsyncTaskManager` destroy).\n\n### Gaps I could not close\n- Exact line numbers for `BrowserPage.close()`, `DetachedBrowserPage.close()`, `BrowserFrame.abort()`, and the `BrowserWindow` timer/rAF registration bodies.\n- The exact test command (I had not yet run `python -m pytest -q` — note this repo is TypeScript/Vitest, so the pytest instruction likely does not apply; the harness is almost certainly `npm test` / `npx vitest run` inside `packages/happy-dom`).\n- Whether `Response.formData()` has a separate code path from `FetchBodyUtility`.\n\nRecommendation: re-run this recon step with tool access restored, specifically to (1) capture the close/abort line numbers, (2) confirm the test runner command, and (3) verify `formData()` routing — then proceed to implementation.' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 1275, 'prompt_tokens': 24089, 'total_tokens': 25364, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 23936}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 23936, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 153}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6', 'id': '39601afc-9cfe-4449-a207-ca43eec870c6', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None} id='lc_run--01a218df-2eb8-73b3-8bc4-a500384c17f2-0' tool_calls=[] invalid_tool_calls=[] usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 24089, 'output_tokens': 1275, 'total_tokens': 25364, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 23936}, 'output_token_details': {}}
